.TH WAVE-TRANSFER 1 "" "LinuxWave" "LinuxWave Manual"

.SH NAME
wave-transfer \- Rewrite the RPATH of already installed ELF files so they no longer name an absolute install path, then leave them ready to run from anywhere. Packages that are already relative are detected and skipped, so the command is safe to repeat. Dependencies used by the named packages are transferred too, otherwise the tree still could not be moved.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wave transfer <package>[@<version>] [, ...] | wave transfer \-\-all
.SH DESCRIPTION
Rewrite the RPATH of already installed ELF files so they no longer name
an absolute install path, then leave them ready to run from anywhere.
Packages that are already relative are detected and skipped, so the
command is safe to repeat. Dependencies used by the named packages are
transferred too, otherwise the tree still could not be moved.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-all
Transfer every installed package and dependency
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-dry\-run
Only report which packages would be transferred

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
wave transfer jq
wave transfer jq, yq
wave transfer --all --dry-run
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
wave(1)
